# Backtest of live inference on the post-May gap (2026-05-28 to 2026-09-19)
115 days, 4438 GB+IRE races, 41381 runners. Walk-forward with fast_inference.py: each day is predicted from history = raceform.db (to 2026-05-27) plus every earlier day's results, with the day's own result columns blanked. Features verified identical to the training matrix. `rpr`/`ts` are NULL for the gap days (prior_rpr/prior_ts do not see them).

## Headline (#1 pick per race, blend_all)
| metric | value | 95% CI (race bootstrap) | held-out reference |
|---|---|---|---|
| top-1 (pick won) | 0.279 | 0.266 to 0.292 | 0.273 |
| top-3 (pick placed) | 0.595 | 0.581 to 0.609 | ~0.60 |
| precision@3 | 0.522 | 0.514 to 0.530 | |
| MRR of the winner | 0.490 | | ~0.49 |
| mean position error | 2.760 | | random ~3.5 |
| runner AUC (win) | 0.7389 | | 0.7445 |
| average precision (win) | 0.275 | 0.258 to 0.294 | ~0.27 |
| base win rate per runner | 0.107 | | |
| race log-loss (runner, blend_all) | 0.303 | | |

